{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-electron-knot","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:electron-knot","kind":"definition","title":"Electron","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-up-quark","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-knot-particle-dictionary"],"tags":["electron","lepton","hopf-link","braid-word","fermion"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Archimedean.Electron","text":"electron-knot.md","leanSource":"electron-knot.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:electron-knot\"></a><p>The <strong>electron</strong> is the braid word</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  e^- = \\sigma_0\\sigma_1\\sigma_0 \\in B_3 ,</code></pre>\n<p>whose image in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_3(q)</code> is the longest basis element <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{w_0}</code>. Its closure is the positive Hopf link: the word permutes the three strands by a transposition, so the closure has two components, with linking number <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+1</code>.</p>\n<p>It is the lepton partner of the <a href=\"#def:up-quark\" data-at=\"knots-particles-confinement/nucleon-derivation\">up quark</a> in the <a href=\"#rem:knot-particle-dictionary\" data-at=\"knots-particles-confinement/skein-particle-generation\">knot–particle dictionary</a>.</p>\n<p>Only the braid word is fixed here. The numerical value of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">m_e</code> is CAL-1, the leptonic mass-scale input used to normalize the observable tower; it is not derived from the word.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/electron-knot.md","heading":"Definition","number":"16.1.1","page":"b/def-electron-knot","qa":{"counts":{"pass":82,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":10,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.MassTheory.Archimedean.Electron","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/electron-knot.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
